Help Type: topic
Topic: file-import

Source Files and Provenance

Purpose:
  Put source-file content into a `.wikg` archive while keeping normalized text
  traceable to the file and location that produced it.

Built-in EPUB import:
  {{ commandName }} wikg://book.wikg create --import ./book.epub
  - `create --import` currently accepts EPUB and creates its chapter structure,
    source text, and source-text map.

External extractor input:
  {{ commandName }} wikg://book.wikg/chapter add --title "Part" --json
  {{ commandName }} <locatedUri>/source set --input ./source.jsonl --input-format jsonl
  - Use this path for PDF, or when another extractor handles EPUB.
  - Chapter paths are returned handles, not title-derived slugs. Reuse `locatedUri`
    from the first command; the selected chapter must be `planned`.

JSONL contract:
  - Each non-empty line is one `artifact` or `text` object. At least one of each is required.
  - An artifact record is `{"type":"artifact","digest":"<64 hex SHA-256 of source file bytes>","mediaType":"application/pdf|application/epub+zip","name":"<optional>","identifier":"<optional>"}`.
  - A text record is `{"type":"text","text":"...","locator":{...}}` and belongs to the most recently declared artifact.
  - PDF locators are `{"pageIndex":1,"bbox":[left,bottom,right,top]}`; page indexes are 1-based and bbox coordinates are ordered numbers in `[0,1]`.
  - EPUB locators are `{"cfi":"epubcfi(...)"}`.
  - Text records are concatenated exactly in order. WG computes their Unicode character offsets; offsets are not input fields.

Minimal PDF example:
  {"type":"artifact","digest":"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef","mediaType":"application/pdf","name":"book.pdf"}
  {"type":"text","text":"Source text\n","locator":{"pageIndex":1,"bbox":[0,0,1,1]}}

Verification:
  {{ commandName }} <chapter-uri>/source/locators --json
  - This independent scope lists the stored source-text mappings. Read `{{ commandName }} help source-locators` for its range syntax.

Boundaries:
  - OCR, layout analysis, and format-specific extraction belong to the importer; WG consumes the contract above.
  - WG stores normalized source text and its source-text map, not the original PDF or EPUB file.
  - Source text remains usable without a source-text map, but evidence cannot point back to a PDF page or EPUB CFI.
  - Source-file input does not generate Reading Graph, Summary, or Knowledge Graph
    data.

See also:
  - {{ commandName }} wikg://book.wikg create --help
  - {{ commandName }} <chapter-uri>/source set --help
  - {{ commandName }} help format
  - {{ commandName }} help source-locators
